  "id": "COMPOUND:24902 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Phyllofolactones F is implicated in the regulation of VMRC-MELG through a series of mechanistic pathways involving T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3 and other targets. The evidence suggests that Phyllofolactones F acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 2-(1a,4-dimethyl-3,3a,4,5,6,7,7a,7b-octahydro-2H-naphtho[1,2-b]oxiren-7-yl)prop-2-enoic acid and Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-, which both directly target VMRC-MELG. These compounds are likely to exert their effects through interactions with CD3, a key component of the T-cell receptor complex, and thus influence T-cell function. The presence of multiple independent pathways linking Phyllofolactones F to VMRC-MELG suggests a potential role in modulating T-cell activity, possibly through the regulation of CD3-mediated signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that Phyllofolactones F may act as a modulator of VMRC-MELG, potentially through a mechanism involving T-cell surface receptors. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Phyllofolactones F and VMRC-MELG, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
